Isorophida with: center of oral area farmed by three primary orals;
ambulacral coverplates forming single, alternating biseries,
coverplates with both intra-ambulacral and intrathecal extensions;
ambulacral coverplate passageways present; ambulacral floorplates
imbricate; anal area a periproct.

"Lebetodiscidae with: highly convex domal theca; oral area
with several secondary orals; hydropore structure formed by
first three coverplates of ambulacrum Y and one or more
modified interambulacral plates; ambulacra curved, I·Y solar;
coverplate passageways large, external foramina elliptical;
coverplate lateral depression series present."

"A Foerstediscus with: several secondary oral plates;
hydropore structure formed primarily by four plates;
anus near center of interambulacrum 5; thecal plates
covered with large nodes."

"A Foerstediscus with: four or more secondary oral plates;
hydropore structure formed by four plates; peri. proet near
the oral area in proximal part of mteramhu. lacrum 5;
thecal plates smooth,"
